{
 "indicator": {
  "definition": {
   "definition": "The 10-year G-Sec par yield is the semi-annual par yield — the yield a hypothetical Government of India security would carry if priced at par — at the 10-year point of the daily FBIL G-Sec Par Yield Curve. FBIL, designated the RBI's benchmark administrator for government securities with effect from 31 March 2018, derives the curve from transaction-level data on the RBI's NDS-OM platform using a cubic-spline model and publishes G-Sec prices, yields-to-maturity and the par yield curve every Mumbai business day. RBI republishes the figure as '10-Year G-Sec Par Yield (FBIL)' in the WSS/Bulletin, where it is the benchmark long-term sovereign yield.",
   "source_name": "FBIL — G-Sec Par Yield Curve (FBIL newsletter/explanatory notes); RBI circular FMRD.DIRD.7/14.03.025/2017-18",
